Ideas, no code
- freeCodeCamp (https://github.com/freeCodeCamp/freeCodeCamp). Its software is
  BSD-3-Clause; its lessons in /curriculum are copyright freeCodeCamp.org, all
  rights reserved. No code and no lessons were copied. Ideas used: a free,
  open-source curriculum of short lessons, each checked by hidden tests that run
  in the browser.
- boot.dev (https://www.boot.dev), proprietary. No code or content was copied.
  Ideas used: XP and levels, daily streaks, gems, chests, achievements, daily
  quests, a leaderboard, guided multi-step projects, command-line lessons, and an
  AI tutor that gives Socratic hints instead of answers.
- The Win98 look is original CSS and SVG. It uses no Microsoft artwork or fonts;
  it falls back to the system's Tahoma or Verdana.


